  "strategyNotes": [
    "In dialogues, the FINAL agreed plan matters, not the first suggestion. Track changes: 二時 → 三時.",
    "ちょっと… is a polite 'no'. When you see it, expect the plan to change in the next line.",
    "〜ませんか is an invitation; the answer いいですね means acceptance."
